WEBVTT

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:02.820
Hey, Pinky here,

00:00:02.820 --> 00:00:04.120
with a bag of tiles!

00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:07.500
Probability is really just counting.

00:00:08.020 --> 00:00:10.440
The trick is counting the right things.

00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:14.020
Probability is what you want,

00:00:14.020 --> 00:00:16.040
over everything that could happen,

00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:17.360
the sample space.

00:00:17.140 --> 00:00:20.900
As long as every outcome is equally likely.

00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:23.760
Three red tiles.

00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:26.120
Seven blue. Reach in.

00:00:26.120 --> 00:00:27.500
What's the chance of red?

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:30.620
Three red, ten tiles in total.

00:00:30.620 --> 00:00:32.300
Three tenths.

00:00:33.350 --> 00:00:35.590
Your turn. Five red.

00:00:36.070 --> 00:00:38.490
Three blue. What's the chance of blue?

00:00:39.250 --> 00:00:40.150
Go.

00:00:45.570 --> 00:00:48.050
Three eighths! Three blue,

00:00:48.590 --> 00:00:49.490
eight in total.

00:00:50.010 --> 00:00:51.450
If you said three fifths,

00:00:51.610 --> 00:00:53.310
you left the blues out of the total.

00:00:55.250 --> 00:00:57.430
Now watch what happens when I draw a red tile,

00:00:57.430 --> 00:00:58.990
and I don't put it back.

00:00:59.530 --> 00:01:00.450
The bag changes.

00:01:00.790 --> 00:01:02.170
Two red left,

00:01:02.870 --> 00:01:03.910
nine tiles in total.

00:01:04.610 --> 00:01:07.130
The chance of red is now two ninths,

00:01:07.130 --> 00:01:08.490
not three tenths.

00:01:08.690 --> 00:01:10.410
These draws aren't independent.

00:01:11.010 --> 00:01:12.510
The second depends on the first.

00:01:13.990 --> 00:01:16.050
For at least one,

00:01:16.590 --> 00:01:17.490
flip it around:

00:01:18.090 --> 00:01:20.050
one minus the chance of none.

00:01:20.830 --> 00:01:21.730
Flip a coin twice.

00:01:22.190 --> 00:01:23.270
At least one heads?

00:01:23.910 --> 00:01:24.810
Don't count them all.

00:01:25.350 --> 00:01:27.130
The only way to fail is tails,

00:01:27.130 --> 00:01:28.790
tails. That's one fourth.

00:01:29.170 --> 00:01:31.330
So one minus one fourth:

00:01:31.950 --> 00:01:33.510
three fourths.

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:36.000
So read the little words.

00:01:36.680 --> 00:01:38.780
Given that. Without replacement.

00:01:39.380 --> 00:01:41.560
At least. They tell you what to count.

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:43.780
Now hit Try this skill!
